    <string name="seekerog_syntax_help">Typed in the SEARCH box: plain words and -exclusions go to the Soulseek server; everything else filters the results locally.\nTyped in the FILTER box: everything filters the current results.\n\nFORMAT  format:flac  format:flac,mp3  ext:m4a  lossless  lossy  hires\nQUALITY  bitrate:320 (min)  bitrate>=256  bitrate:192-256  samplerate:96k  bits:24\nSIZE  size&lt;100MB  size>=1.5GB  size:10-50 (MB)\nDURATION  dur:3:30 (±5 s)  dur:3:30~10  dur>=2m  dur:3:00-4:00\nAVAILABILITY  free:yes  queue&lt;=10  speed>=500kb  files>=8  fav:yes  downloaded:no\nTEXT  \"exact phrase\"  -word  -\"phrase\"  word*  user:name  folder:name  file:name  artist:\"Daft Punk\"  album:Discovery\nREGEX  re:/\\(19[89]\\d\\)/  (case-insensitive; add c after the last / for case sensitive)\n\nOperators: : = &gt; &gt;= &lt; &lt;= ~ and ranges a-b. Spanish aliases work too (formato, frecuencia, profundidad, tamaño, duracion, cola, velocidad, usuario, carpeta, archivo, artista).\nMetadata the peer did not send (bitrate, sample rate, depth, duration) is unknown and does not match quality filters. artist/album/title match the folder and file names because Soulseek results contain no tags.</string>
